  ('77777777-0000-0000-0000-000000000066', 1, 'Main', 'When should you use the Strategy pattern? Give an example.', 'Use Strategy when there are several ways to do the same job and you want to choose one at runtime without a chain of if-else statements. You define an interface, each algorithm is a class implementing it, and the client only holds the interface. For example, shipping fee calculation with one strategy per carrier, selected from the carrier the customer picks.', 'audio/000019/q4-t1.webm', timestamptz '2026-09-15 12:30+07' + interval '541 seconds', timestamptz '2026-09-15 12:30+07' + interval '654 seconds'),
  ('77777777-0000-0000-0000-000000000067', 1, 'Main', 'Explain the difference between a layered architecture and Clean Architecture.', 'Clean Architecture means clean code with clear variable names.', 'audio/000020/q1-t1.webm', timestamptz '2026-09-15 13:00+07' + interval '30 seconds', timestamptz '2026-09-15 13:00+07' + interval '144 seconds'),
  ('77777777-0000-0000-0000-000000000067', 2, 'FollowUp', 'In Clean Architecture, which layer should the repository interface live in? Why?', 'In the data layer.', 'audio/000020/q1-t2.webm', timestamptz '2026-09-15 13:00+07' + interval '154 seconds', timestamptz '2026-09-15 13:00+07' + interval '247 seconds'),
  ('77777777-0000-0000-0000-000000000067', 3, 'FollowUp', 'Could you give a concrete example to illustrate that?', 'Sorry, I cannot think of an example.', 'audio/000020/q1-t3.webm', timestamptz '2026-09-15 13:00+07' + interval '257 seconds', timestamptz '2026-09-15 13:00+07' + interval '328 seconds'),
  ('77777777-0000-0000-0000-000000000068', 1, 'Main', 'Explain the Repository and Unit of Work patterns. Should you use them with EF Core?', 'A repository is where you store code on GitHub.', 'audio/000020/q2-t1.webm', timestamptz '2026-09-15 13:00+07' + interval '338 seconds', timestamptz '2026-09-15 13:00+07' + interval '431 seconds'),
  ('77777777-0000-0000-0000-000000000068', 2, 'FollowUp', 'What role does EF Core''s DbContext play with respect to Unit of Work?', 'I am not really sure.', 'audio/000020/q2-t2.webm', timestamptz '2026-09-15 13:00+07' + interval '441 seconds', timestamptz '2026-09-15 13:00+07' + interval '485 seconds'),
  ('77777777-0000-0000-0000-000000000068', 3, 'FollowUp', 'Could you give a concrete example to illustrate that?', 'Sorry, I cannot think of an example.', 'audio/000020/q2-t3.webm', timestamptz '2026-09-15 13:00+07' + interval '495 seconds', timestamptz '2026-09-15 13:00+07' + interval '590 seconds'),
  ('77777777-0000-0000-0000-000000000069', 1, 'Main', 'What are coupling and cohesion? Give an example of a highly cohesive design.', 'Coupling is classes depending on each other and should be low. Cohesion is a class doing one thing and should be high.', 'audio/000020/q3-t1.webm', timestamptz '2026-09-15 13:00+07' + interval '600 seconds', timestamptz '2026-09-15 13:00+07' + interval '647 seconds'),
  ('77777777-0000-0000-0000-000000000069', 2, 'FollowUp', 'Can you give a concrete example of high cohesion?', 'For example, an EmailSender class that only has methods for sending emails.', 'audio/000020/q3-t2.webm', timestamptz '2026-09-15 13:00+07' + interval '657 seconds', timestamptz '2026-09-15 13:00+07' + interval '700 seconds'),
  ('77777777-0000-0000-0000-000000000070', 1, 'Main', 'When should you use the Strategy pattern? Give an example.', 'When there are several interchangeable algorithms, for example several payment methods.', 'audio/000020/q4-t1.webm', timestamptz '2026-09-15 13:00+07' + interval '710 seconds', timestamptz '2026-09-15 13:00+07' + interval '775 seconds'),
  ('77777777-0000-0000-0000-000000000070', 2, 'FollowUp', 'How does Strategy help compared with writing if-else?', 'You can add a new option without changing existing code, which follows the open-closed principle.', 'audio/000020/q4-t2.webm', timestamptz '2026-09-15 13:00+07' + interval '785 seconds', timestamptz '2026-09-15 13:00+07' + interval '842 seconds'),
  ('77777777-0000-0000-0000-000000000071', 1, 'Main', 'Explain the difference between a layered architecture and Clean Architecture.', 'A layered architecture has Presentation, Business and Data layers with dependencies flowing downward, so business logic usually depends on data access. Clean Architecture puts the Domain and use cases at the center; outer layers like the UI and the database are details that depend inward through interfaces. For example, the repository interface lives in Application and the EF Core implementation lives in Infrastructure.', 'audio/000021/q1-t1.webm', timestamptz '2026-09-15 13:30+07' + interval '30 seconds', timestamptz '2026-09-15 13:30+07' + interval '70 seconds'),
  ('77777777-0000-0000-0000-000000000072', 1, 'Main', 'Explain the Repository and Unit of Work patterns. Should you use them with EF Core?', 'A repository is the data access layer, and Unit of Work saves several changes together in one transaction. You can use them with EF Core.', 'audio/000021/q2-t1.webm', timestamptz '2026-09-15 13:30+07' + interval '80 seconds', timestamptz '2026-09-15 13:30+07' + interval '184 seconds'),
  ('77777777-0000-0000-0000-000000000072', 2, 'FollowUp', 'What role does EF Core''s DbContext play with respect to Unit of Work?', 'DbContext tracks changes and SaveChanges commits them at once, so it works like a Unit of Work.', 'audio/000021/q2-t2.webm', timestamptz '2026-09-15 13:30+07' + interval '194 seconds', timestamptz '2026-09-15 13:30+07' + interval '303 seconds'),
  ('77777777-0000-0000-0000-000000000073', 1, 'Main', 'What are coupling and cohesion? Give an example of a highly cohesive design.', 'Coupling means merging two classes to keep the code short.', 'audio/000021/q3-t1.webm', timestamptz '2026-09-15 13:30+07' + interval '313 seconds', timestamptz '2026-09-15 13:30+07' + interval '404 seconds'),
  ('77777777-0000-0000-0000-000000000073', 2, 'FollowUp', 'Can you give a concrete example of high cohesion?', 'A class that has many methods.', 'audio/000021/q3-t2.webm', timestamptz '2026-09-15 13:30+07' + interval '414 seconds', timestamptz '2026-09-15 13:30+07' + interval '467 seconds'),
  ('77777777-0000-0000-0000-000000000073', 3, 'FollowUp', 'Could you give a concrete example to illustrate that?', NULL, NULL, timestamptz '2026-09-15 13:30+07' + interval '477 seconds', NULL),
  ('77777777-0000-0000-0000-000000000074', 1, 'Main', 'When should you use the Strategy pattern? Give an example.', 'Use Strategy when there are several ways to do the same job and you want to choose one at runtime without a chain of if-else statements. You define an interface, each algorithm is a class implementing it, and the client only holds the interface. For example, shipping fee calculation with one strategy per carrier, selected from the carrier the customer picks.', 'audio/000021/q4-t1.webm', timestamptz '2026-09-15 13:30+07' + interval '607 seconds', timestamptz '2026-09-15 13:30+07' + interval '670 seconds'),
  ('77777777-0000-0000-0000-000000000075', 1, 'Main', 'Describe the normal forms 1NF, 2NF and 3NF and give an example that violates 2NF.', '1NF means single values, 2NF means depending on the whole key, 3NF means no transitive dependencies.', 'audio/000022/q1-t1.webm', now() - interval '40 hours' + interval '30 seconds', now() - interval '40 hours' + interval '99 seconds'),
  ('77777777-0000-0000-0000-000000000075', 2, 'FollowUp', 'Can you give an example of a table that violates 2NF?', 'A table keyed by OrderId and ProductId that also stores ProductName, which depends only on ProductId.', 'audio/000022/q1-t2.webm', now() - interval '40 hours' + interval '109 seconds', now() - interval '40 hours' + interval '166 seconds'),
  ('77777777-0000-0000-0000-000000000076', 1, 'Main', 'Explain the difference between INNER JOIN and LEFT JOIN, and give an example of when to use LEFT JOIN.', 'LEFT JOIN joins the table that is on the left of the screen.', 'audio/000022/q2-t1.webm', now() - interval '40 hours' + interval '176 seconds', now() - interval '40 hours' + interval '241 seconds'),
  ('77777777-0000-0000-0000-000000000076', 2, 'FollowUp', 'Can you give a concrete situation that requires a LEFT JOIN?', 'When you want more data.', 'audio/000022/q2-t2.webm', now() - interval '40 hours' + interval '251 seconds', now() - interval '40 hours' + interval '305 seconds'),
  ('77777777-0000-0000-0000-000000000076', 3, 'FollowUp', 'Could you give a concrete example to illustrate that?', 'Sorry, I cannot think of an example.', 'audio/000022/q2-t3.webm', now() - interval '40 hours' + interval '315 seconds', now() - interval '40 hours' + interval '355 seconds'),
  ('77777777-0000-0000-0000-000000000077', 1, 'Main', 'What is an index? When can an index slow the system down?', 'An index is the row number in a table.', 'audio/000022/q3-t1.webm', now() - interval '40 hours' + interval '365 seconds', now() - interval '40 hours' + interval '419 seconds'),
  ('77777777-0000-0000-0000-000000000077', 2, 'FollowUp', 'Why does an index make writes slower?', 'Because the table has a lot of data.', 'audio/000022/q3-t2.webm', now() - interval '40 hours' + interval '429 seconds', now() - interval '40 hours' + interval '474 seconds'),
  ('77777777-0000-0000-0000-000000000077', 3, 'FollowUp', 'Could you give a concrete example to illustrate that?', 'Sorry, I cannot think of an example.', 'audio/000022/q3-t3.webm', now() - interval '40 hours' + interval '484 seconds', now() - interval '40 hours' + interval '560 seconds'),
  ('77777777-0000-0000-0000-000000000078', 1, 'Main', 'Explain the ACID properties of a transaction.', 'ACID is an acid from chemistry.', 'audio/000022/q4-t1.webm', now() - interval '40 hours' + interval '570 seconds', now() - interval '40 hours' + interval '612 seconds'),
  ('77777777-0000-0000-0000-000000000078', 2, 'FollowUp', 'Can you explain Isolation in more detail?', 'It means isolating the data.', 'audio/000022/q4-t2.webm', now() - interval '40 hours' + interval '622 seconds', now() - interval '40 hours' + interval '670 seconds'),
  ('77777777-0000-0000-0000-000000000078', 3, 'FollowUp', 'Could you give a concrete example to illustrate that?', 'Sorry, I cannot think of an example.', 'audio/000022/q4-t3.webm', now() - interval '40 hours' + interval '680 seconds', now() - interval '40 hours' + interval '756 seconds'),
  ('77777777-0000-0000-0000-000000000079', 1, 'Main', 'Describe the normal forms 1NF, 2NF and 3NF and give an example that violates 2NF.', '1NF requires atomic values and no repeating groups. 2NF is 1NF where every non-key attribute depends on the whole primary key. 3NF is 2NF with no transitive dependency on the key. For example, OrderDetail(OrderId, ProductId, Quantity, ProductName) violates 2NF because ProductName depends only on ProductId.', 'audio/000023/q1-t1.webm', now() - interval '34 hours' + interval '30 seconds', now() - interval '34 hours' + interval '115 seconds'),
  ('77777777-0000-0000-0000-000000000080', 1, 'Main', 'Explain the difference between INNER JOIN and LEFT JOIN, and give an example of when to use LEFT JOIN.', 'INNER JOIN takes the common part; LEFT JOIN takes the whole left table even without a match.', 'audio/000023/q2-t1.webm', now() - interval '34 hours' + interval '125 seconds', now() - interval '34 hours' + interval '209 seconds'),
  ('77777777-0000-0000-0000-000000000080', 2, 'FollowUp', 'Can you give a concrete situation that requires a LEFT JOIN?', 'Listing all customers, including those who have not placed any orders.', 'audio/000023/q2-t2.webm', now() - interval '34 hours' + interval '219 seconds', now() - interval '34 hours' + interval '270 seconds'),
  ('77777777-0000-0000-0000-000000000081', 1, 'Main', 'What is an index? When can an index slow the system down?', 'An index is an extra data structure, usually a B-tree, that finds rows by a column without scanning the whole table. It speeds up WHERE, JOIN and ORDER BY, but every INSERT, UPDATE and DELETE must also update the index, so writes get slower and it uses storage. Write-heavy tables or low-selectivity columns gain little from an index.', 'audio/000023/q3-t1.webm', now() - interval '34 hours' + interval '280 seconds', now() - interval '34 hours' + interval '340 seconds'),
  ('77777777-0000-0000-0000-000000000082', 1, 'Main', 'Explain the ACID properties of a transaction.', 'Atomicity means all operations succeed or none take effect. Consistency means the data still satisfies all constraints after the transaction. Isolation means concurrent transactions do not see each other''s partial state, depending on the isolation level. Durability means committed data survives even a power failure.', 'audio/000023/q4-t1.webm', now() - interval '34 hours' + interval '350 seconds', now() - interval '34 hours' + interval '432 seconds'),
  ('77777777-0000-0000-0000-000000000083', 1, 'Main', 'Describe the normal forms 1NF, 2NF and 3NF and give an example that violates 2NF.', '1NF requires atomic values and no repeating groups. 2NF is 1NF where every non-key attribute depends on the whole primary key. 3NF is 2NF with no transitive dependency on the key. For example, OrderDetail(OrderId, ProductId, Quantity, ProductName) violates 2NF because ProductName depends only on ProductId.', 'audio/000024/q1-t1.webm', now() - interval '28 hours' + interval '30 seconds', now() - interval '28 hours' + interval '82 seconds'),
  ('77777777-0000-0000-0000-000000000084', 1, 'Main', 'Explain the difference between INNER JOIN and LEFT JOIN, and give an example of when to use LEFT JOIN.', 'INNER JOIN returns only rows that match in both tables. LEFT JOIN returns every row of the left table, and the right-hand columns are NULL when there is no match. For example, to list all students with their number of attempts, including students with none, use Students LEFT JOIN Attempts and COUNT.', 'audio/000024/q2-t1.webm', now() - interval '28 hours' + interval '92 seconds', now() - interval '28 hours' + interval '168 seconds'),
  ('77777777-0000-0000-0000-000000000085', 1, 'Main', 'What is an index? When can an index slow the system down?', 'An index is an extra data structure, usually a B-tree, that finds rows by a column without scanning the whole table. It speeds up WHERE, JOIN and ORDER BY, but every INSERT, UPDATE and DELETE must also update the index, so writes get slower and it uses storage. Write-heavy tables or low-selectivity columns gain little from an index.', 'audio/000024/q3-t1.webm', now() - interval '28 hours' + interval '178 seconds', now() - interval '28 hours' + interval '234 seconds'),
  ('77777777-0000-0000-0000-000000000086', 1, 'Main', 'Explain the ACID properties of a transaction.', 'Atomicity means all operations succeed or none take effect. Consistency means the data still satisfies all constraints after the transaction. Isolation means concurrent transactions do not see each other''s partial state, depending on the isolation level. Durability means committed data survives even a power failure.', 'audio/000024/q4-t1.webm', now() - interval '28 hours' + interval '244 seconds', now() - interval '28 hours' + interval '302 seconds'),
  ('77777777-0000-0000-0000-000000000087', 1, 'Main', 'Describe the normal forms 1NF, 2NF and 3NF and give an example that violates 2NF.', '1NF means single values, 2NF means depending on the whole key, 3NF means no transitive dependencies.', 'audio/000025/q1-t1.webm', now() - interval '22 hours' + interval '30 seconds', now() - interval '22 hours' + interval '112 seconds'),
  ('77777777-0000-0000-0000-000000000087', 2, 'FollowUp', 'Can you give an example of a table that violates 2NF?', 'A table keyed by OrderId and ProductId that also stores ProductName, which depends only on ProductId.', 'audio/000025/q1-t2.webm', now() - interval '22 hours' + interval '122 seconds', now() - interval '22 hours' + interval '190 seconds'),
  ('77777777-0000-0000-0000-000000000088', 1, 'Main', 'Explain the difference between INNER JOIN and LEFT JOIN, and give an example of when to use LEFT JOIN.', 'LEFT JOIN joins the table that is on the left of the screen.', 'audio/000025/q2-t1.webm', now() - interval '22 hours' + interval '200 seconds', now() - interval '22 hours' + interval '260 seconds'),
  ('77777777-0000-0000-0000-000000000088', 2, 'FollowUp', 'Can you give a concrete situation that requires a LEFT JOIN?', 'When you want more data.', 'audio/000025/q2-t2.webm', now() - interval '22 hours' + interval '270 seconds', now() - interval '22 hours' + interval '315 seconds'),
  ('77777777-0000-0000-0000-000000000088', 3, 'FollowUp', 'Could you give a concrete example to illustrate that?', 'Sorry, I cannot think of an example.', 'audio/000025/q2-t3.webm', now() - interval '22 hours' + interval '325 seconds', now() - interval '22 hours' + interval '395 seconds'),
  ('77777777-0000-0000-0000-000000000089', 1, 'Main', 'What is an index? When can an index slow the system down?', 'An index is the row number in a table.', 'audio/000025/q3-t1.webm', now() - interval '22 hours' + interval '405 seconds', now() - interval '22 hours' + interval '467 seconds'),
  ('77777777-0000-0000-0000-000000000089', 2, 'FollowUp', 'Why does an index make writes slower?', 'Because the table has a lot of data.', 'audio/000025/q3-t2.webm', now() - interval '22 hours' + interval '477 seconds', now() - interval '22 hours' + interval '524 seconds'),
  ('77777777-0000-0000-0000-000000000089', 3, 'FollowUp', 'Could you give a concrete example to illustrate that?', NULL, NULL, now() - interval '22 hours' + interval '534 seconds', NULL),
  ('77777777-0000-0000-0000-000000000090', 1, 'Main', 'Explain the ACID properties of a transaction.', 'ACID is an acid from chemistry.', 'audio/000025/q4-t1.webm', now() - interval '22 hours' + interval '634 seconds', now() - interval '22 hours' + interval '678 seconds'),
  ('77777777-0000-0000-0000-000000000090', 2, 'FollowUp', 'Can you explain Isolation in more detail?', 'It means isolating the data.', 'audio/000025/q4-t2.webm', now() - interval '22 hours' + interval '688 seconds', now() - interval '22 hours' + interval '747 seconds'),
  ('77777777-0000-0000-0000-000000000090', 3, 'FollowUp', 'Could you give a concrete example to illustrate that?', NULL, NULL, now() - interval '22 hours' + interval '757 seconds', NULL),
  ('77777777-0000-0000-0000-000000000091', 1, 'Main', 'Describe the normal forms 1NF, 2NF and 3NF and give an example that violates 2NF.', '1NF requires atomic values and no repeating groups. 2NF is 1NF where every non-key attribute depends on the whole primary key. 3NF is 2NF with no transitive dependency on the key. For example, OrderDetail(OrderId, ProductId, Quantity, ProductName) violates 2NF because ProductName depends only on ProductId.', 'audio/000026/q1-t1.webm', now() - interval '16 hours' + interval '30 seconds', now() - interval '16 hours' + interval '96 seconds'),
  ('77777777-0000-0000-0000-000000000092', 1, 'Main', 'Explain the difference between INNER JOIN and LEFT JOIN, and give an example of when to use LEFT JOIN.', 'INNER JOIN takes the common part; LEFT JOIN takes the whole left table even without a match.', 'audio/000026/q2-t1.webm', now() - interval '16 hours' + interval '106 seconds', now() - interval '16 hours' + interval '169 seconds'),
  ('77777777-0000-0000-0000-000000000092', 2, 'FollowUp', 'Can you give a concrete situation that requires a LEFT JOIN?', 'Listing all customers, including those who have not placed any orders.', 'audio/000026/q2-t2.webm', now() - interval '16 hours' + interval '179 seconds', now() - interval '16 hours' + interval '254 seconds'),
  ('77777777-0000-0000-0000-000000000093', 1, 'Main', 'What is an index? When can an index slow the system down?', 'An index makes searching faster, like a book''s table of contents, but too many indexes slow down inserts.', 'audio/000026/q3-t1.webm', now() - interval '16 hours' + interval '264 seconds', now() - interval '16 hours' + interval '306 seconds'),
  ('77777777-0000-0000-0000-000000000093', 2, 'FollowUp', 'Why does an index make writes slower?', 'Because every write must also update the index structure.', 'audio/000026/q3-t2.webm', now() - interval '16 hours' + interval '316 seconds', now() - interval '16 hours' + interval '362 seconds'),
  ('77777777-0000-0000-0000-000000000094', 1, 'Main', 'Explain the ACID properties of a transaction.', 'Atomicity is all or nothing and durability means committed data is not lost; I do not remember consistency and isolation well.', 'audio/000026/q4-t1.webm', now() - interval '16 hours' + interval '372 seconds', now() - interval '16 hours' + interval '452 seconds'),
  ('77777777-0000-0000-0000-000000000094', 2, 'FollowUp', 'Can you explain Isolation in more detail?', 'Isolation means transactions running at the same time do not affect each other.', 'audio/000026/q4-t2.webm', now() - interval '16 hours' + interval '462 seconds', now() - interval '16 hours' + interval '527 seconds'),
  ('77777777-0000-0000-0000-000000000095', 1, 'Main', 'Explain the difference between black-box and white-box testing.', 'Black-box testing is based on the specification without knowing the code, using techniques like equivalence partitioning and boundary value analysis. White-box testing is based on the code structure, for example statement coverage and branch coverage. Black-box tests are usually written by testers, white-box tests by developers when writing unit tests.', 'audio/000027/q1-t1.webm', timestamptz '2026-09-22 08:00+07' + interval '30 seconds', timestamptz '2026-09-22 08:00+07' + interval '113 seconds'),
  ('77777777-0000-0000-0000-000000000096', 1, 'Main', 'Explain equivalence partitioning and boundary value analysis, with an example.', 'It means testing many times to be sure.', 'audio/000027/q2-t1.webm', timestamptz '2026-09-22 08:00+07' + interval '123 seconds', timestamptz '2026-09-22 08:00+07' + interval '194 seconds'),
  ('77777777-0000-0000-0000-000000000096', 2, 'FollowUp', 'For an age field from 18 to 60, which boundary values would you pick?', 'I would pick 18 and 60.', 'audio/000027/q2-t2.webm', timestamptz '2026-09-22 08:00+07' + interval '204 seconds', timestamptz '2026-09-22 08:00+07' + interval '313 seconds'),
  ('77777777-0000-0000-0000-000000000097', 1, 'Main', 'How is a unit test different from an integration test? Why do we need mocks?', 'A unit test tests one function; an integration test tests several parts together. Mocks fake the data.', 'audio/000027/q3-t1.webm', timestamptz '2026-09-22 08:00+07' + interval '323 seconds', timestamptz '2026-09-22 08:00+07' + interval '394 seconds'),
  ('77777777-0000-0000-0000-000000000097', 2, 'FollowUp', 'How do mocks help unit tests?', 'They remove the dependency on the database, so tests run fast and give stable results.', 'audio/000027/q3-t2.webm', timestamptz '2026-09-22 08:00+07' + interval '404 seconds', timestamptz '2026-09-22 08:00+07' + interval '455 seconds'),
  ('77777777-0000-0000-0000-000000000098', 1, 'Main', 'What information should a good bug report contain?', 'It needs a title, the steps taken and the wrong result.', 'audio/000027/q4-t1.webm', timestamptz '2026-09-22 08:00+07' + interval '465 seconds', timestamptz '2026-09-22 08:00+07' + interval '558 seconds'),
  ('77777777-0000-0000-0000-000000000098', 2, 'FollowUp', 'Besides the steps to reproduce, what information about the environment does a bug report need?', 'The browser, the operating system and the application version.', 'audio/000027/q4-t2.webm', timestamptz '2026-09-22 08:00+07' + interval '568 seconds', timestamptz '2026-09-22 08:00+07' + interval '619 seconds'),
  ('77777777-0000-0000-0000-000000000099', 1, 'Main', 'Explain the difference between black-box and white-box testing.', 'Black-box testing is based on the specification without knowing the code, using techniques like equivalence partitioning and boundary value analysis. White-box testing is based on the code structure, for example statement coverage and branch coverage. Black-box tests are usually written by testers, white-box tests by developers when writing unit tests.', 'audio/000028/q1-t1.webm', timestamptz '2026-09-22 08:30+07' + interval '30 seconds', timestamptz '2026-09-22 08:30+07' + interval '91 seconds'),
  ('77777777-0000-0000-0000-000000000100', 1, 'Main', 'Explain equivalence partitioning and boundary value analysis, with an example.', 'Partitioning splits the inputs into groups and tests one value per group. Boundary values test the start and end of a range.', 'audio/000028/q2-t1.webm', timestamptz '2026-09-22 08:30+07' + interval '101 seconds', timestamptz '2026-09-22 08:30+07' + interval '188 seconds'),
  ('77777777-0000-0000-0000-000000000100', 2, 'FollowUp', 'For an age field from 18 to 60, which boundary values would you pick?', 'I would pick 17, 18, 60 and 61.', 'audio/000028/q2-t2.webm', timestamptz '2026-09-22 08:30+07' + interval '198 seconds', timestamptz '2026-09-22 08:30+07' + interval '253 seconds'),
  ('77777777-0000-0000-0000-000000000101', 1, 'Main', 'How is a unit test different from an integration test? Why do we need mocks?', 'A unit test checks a small unit such as one function or class; it is fast and isolated. An integration test checks several components working together, such as the API with a real database. Mocks replace external dependencies like the database or an AI service, so unit tests stay isolated, fast and stable.', 'audio/000028/q3-t1.webm', timestamptz '2026-09-22 08:30+07' + interval '263 seconds', timestamptz '2026-09-22 08:30+07' + interval '335 seconds'),
  ('77777777-0000-0000-0000-000000000102', 1, 'Main', 'What information should a good bug report contain?', 'Just write that there is a bug.', 'audio/000028/q4-t1.webm', timestamptz '2026-09-22 08:30+07' + interval '345 seconds', timestamptz '2026-09-22 08:30+07' + interval '408 seconds'),
  ('77777777-0000-0000-0000-000000000102', 2, 'FollowUp', 'Besides the steps to reproduce, what information about the environment does a bug report need?', 'That is not needed.', 'audio/000028/q4-t2.webm', timestamptz '2026-09-22 08:30+07' + interval '418 seconds', timestamptz '2026-09-22 08:30+07' + interval '458 seconds'),
  ('77777777-0000-0000-0000-000000000103', 1, 'Main', 'Explain the difference between black-box and white-box testing.', 'Black-box testing is testing at night.', 'audio/000029/q1-t1.webm', timestamptz '2026-09-22 09:00+07' + interval '30 seconds', timestamptz '2026-09-22 09:00+07' + interval '125 seconds'),
  ('77777777-0000-0000-0000-000000000103', 2, 'FollowUp', 'Can you name one technique for each type?', 'I have not studied this part well.', 'audio/000029/q1-t2.webm', timestamptz '2026-09-22 09:00+07' + interval '135 seconds', timestamptz '2026-09-22 09:00+07' + interval '179 seconds'),
  ('77777777-0000-0000-0000-000000000104', 1, 'Main', 'Explain equivalence partitioning and boundary value analysis, with an example.', 'Equivalence partitioning splits the input domain into classes that the system treats the same way and picks one representative per class. Boundary value analysis tests at and next to the boundaries, where bugs are common. For an age field valid from 18 to 60: valid class 30, invalid classes 10 and 70; boundary tests 17, 18, 60 and 61.', 'audio/000029/q2-t1.webm', timestamptz '2026-09-22 09:00+07' + interval '189 seconds', timestamptz '2026-09-22 09:00+07' + interval '260 seconds'),
  ('77777777-0000-0000-0000-000000000105', 1, 'Main', 'How is a unit test different from an integration test? Why do we need mocks?', 'A unit test tests one function; an integration test tests several parts together. Mocks fake the data.', 'audio/000029/q3-t1.webm', timestamptz '2026-09-22 09:00+07' + interval '270 seconds', timestamptz '2026-09-22 09:00+07' + interval '385 seconds'),
  ('77777777-0000-0000-0000-000000000105', 2, 'FollowUp', 'How do mocks help unit tests?', 'They remove the dependency on the database, so tests run fast and give stable results.', 'audio/000029/q3-t2.webm', timestamptz '2026-09-22 09:00+07' + interval '395 seconds', timestamptz '2026-09-22 09:00+07' + interval '484 seconds'),
  ('77777777-0000-0000-0000-000000000106', 1, 'Main', 'What information should a good bug report contain?', 'It needs a title, the steps taken and the wrong result.', 'audio/000029/q4-t1.webm', timestamptz '2026-09-22 09:00+07' + interval '494 seconds', timestamptz '2026-09-22 09:00+07' + interval '609 seconds'),
  ('77777777-0000-0000-0000-000000000106', 2, 'FollowUp', 'Besides the steps to reproduce, what information about the environment does a bug report need?', 'The browser, the operating system and the application version.', 'audio/000029/q4-t2.webm', timestamptz '2026-09-22 09:00+07' + interval '619 seconds', timestamptz '2026-09-22 09:00+07' + interval '718 seconds'),
  ('77777777-0000-0000-0000-000000000107', 1, 'Main', 'Explain the difference between black-box and white-box testing.', 'Black-box testing is testing at night.', 'audio/000030/q1-t1.webm', timestamptz '2026-09-22 09:30+07' + interval '30 seconds', timestamptz '2026-09-22 09:30+07' + interval '118 seconds'),
  ('77777777-0000-0000-0000-000000000107', 2, 'FollowUp', 'Can you name one technique for each type?', 'I have not studied this part well.', 'audio/000030/q1-t2.webm', timestamptz '2026-09-22 09:30+07' + interval '128 seconds', timestamptz '2026-09-22 09:30+07' + interval '229 seconds'),
  ('77777777-0000-0000-0000-000000000108', 1, 'Main', 'Explain equivalence partitioning and boundary value analysis, with an example.', 'Partitioning splits the inputs into groups and tests one value per group. Boundary values test the start and end of a range.', 'audio/000030/q2-t1.webm', timestamptz '2026-09-22 09:30+07' + interval '239 seconds', timestamptz '2026-09-22 09:30+07' + interval '350 seconds'),
  ('77777777-0000-0000-0000-000000000108', 2, 'FollowUp', 'For an age field from 18 to 60, which boundary values would you pick?', 'I would pick 17, 18, 60 and 61.', 'audio/000030/q2-t2.webm', timestamptz '2026-09-22 09:30+07' + interval '360 seconds', timestamptz '2026-09-22 09:30+07' + interval '439 seconds'),
  ('77777777-0000-0000-0000-000000000109', 1, 'Main', 'How is a unit test different from an integration test? Why do we need mocks?', 'A unit test checks a small unit such as one function or class; it is fast and isolated. An integration test checks several components working together, such as the API with a real database. Mocks replace external dependencies like the database or an AI service, so unit tests stay isolated, fast and stable.', 'audio/000030/q3-t1.webm', timestamptz '2026-09-22 09:30+07' + interval '449 seconds', timestamptz '2026-09-22 09:30+07' + interval '519 seconds'),
  ('77777777-0000-0000-0000-000000000110', 1, 'Main', 'What information should a good bug report contain?', 'It needs a title, the steps taken and the wrong result.', 'audio/000030/q4-t1.webm', timestamptz '2026-09-22 09:30+07' + interval '529 seconds', timestamptz '2026-09-22 09:30+07' + interval '599 seconds'),
  ('77777777-0000-0000-0000-000000000110', 2, 'FollowUp', 'Besides the steps to reproduce, what information about the environment does a bug report need?', 'The browser, the operating system and the application version.', 'audio/000030/q4-t2.webm', timestamptz '2026-09-22 09:30+07' + interval '609 seconds', timestamptz '2026-09-22 09:30+07' + interval '656 seconds'),
  ('77777777-0000-0000-0000-000000000111', 1, 'Main', 'Explain the difference between black-box and white-box testing.', 'Black-box means testing features without looking at the code. White-box means looking at the code to test it.', 'audio/000031/q1-t1.webm', timestamptz '2026-09-22 10:00+07' + interval '30 seconds', timestamptz '2026-09-22 10:00+07' + interval '110 seconds'),
  ('77777777-0000-0000-0000-000000000111', 2, 'FollowUp', 'Can you name one technique for each type?', 'Boundary values for black-box, branch coverage for white-box.', 'audio/000031/q1-t2.webm', timestamptz '2026-09-22 10:00+07' + interval '120 seconds', timestamptz '2026-09-22 10:00+07' + interval '179 seconds'),
  ('77777777-0000-0000-0000-000000000112', 1, 'Main', 'Explain equivalence partitioning and boundary value analysis, with an example.', 'Partitioning splits the inputs into groups and tests one value per group. Boundary values test the start and end of a range.', 'audio/000031/q2-t1.webm', timestamptz '2026-09-22 10:00+07' + interval '189 seconds', timestamptz '2026-09-22 10:00+07' + interval '274 seconds'),
  ('77777777-0000-0000-0000-000000000112', 2, 'FollowUp', 'For an age field from 18 to 60, which boundary values would you pick?', 'I would pick 17, 18, 60 and 61.', 'audio/000031/q2-t2.webm', timestamptz '2026-09-22 10:00+07' + interval '284 seconds', timestamptz '2026-09-22 10:00+07' + interval '399 seconds'),
  ('77777777-0000-0000-0000-000000000113', 1, 'Main', 'How is a unit test different from an integration test? Why do we need mocks?', 'A unit test tests one function; an integration test tests several parts together. Mocks fake the data.', 'audio/000031/q3-t1.webm', timestamptz '2026-09-22 10:00+07' + interval '409 seconds', timestamptz '2026-09-22 10:00+07' + interval '472 seconds'),
  ('77777777-0000-0000-0000-000000000113', 2, 'FollowUp', 'How do mocks help unit tests?', 'They remove the dependency on the database, so tests run fast and give stable results.', 'audio/000031/q3-t2.webm', timestamptz '2026-09-22 10:00+07' + interval '482 seconds', timestamptz '2026-09-22 10:00+07' + interval '574 seconds'),
  ('77777777-0000-0000-0000-000000000114', 1, 'Main', 'What information should a good bug report contain?', 'A bug report needs a clear title, steps to reproduce, the expected and actual results, the environment such as browser and version, severity and priority, and screenshots or logs.', 'audio/000031/q4-t1.webm', timestamptz '2026-09-22 10:00+07' + interval '584 seconds', timestamptz '2026-09-22 10:00+07' + interval '653 seconds'),
  ('77777777-0000-0000-0000-000000000115', 1, 'Main', 'Explain the difference between black-box and white-box testing.', 'Black-box testing is testing at night.', 'audio/000032/q1-t1.webm', timestamptz '2026-09-22 10:30+07' + interval '30 seconds', timestamptz '2026-09-22 10:30+07' + interval '119 seconds'),
  ('77777777-0000-0000-0000-000000000115', 2, 'FollowUp', 'Can you name one technique for each type?', 'I have not studied this part well.', 'audio/000032/q1-t2.webm', timestamptz '2026-09-22 10:30+07' + interval '129 seconds', timestamptz '2026-09-22 10:30+07' + interval '226 seconds'),
  ('77777777-0000-0000-0000-000000000116', 1, 'Main', 'Explain equivalence partitioning and boundary value analysis, with an example.', 'Equivalence partitioning splits the input domain into classes that the system treats the same way and picks one representative per class. Boundary value analysis tests at and next to the boundaries, where bugs are common. For an age field valid from 18 to 60: valid class 30, invalid classes 10 and 70; boundary tests 17, 18, 60 and 61.', 'audio/000032/q2-t1.webm', timestamptz '2026-09-22 10:30+07' + interval '236 seconds', timestamptz '2026-09-22 10:30+07' + interval '285 seconds'),
  ('77777777-0000-0000-0000-000000000117', 1, 'Main', 'How is a unit test different from an integration test? Why do we need mocks?', 'A unit test is a UI test.', 'audio/000032/q3-t1.webm', timestamptz '2026-09-22 10:30+07' + interval '295 seconds', timestamptz '2026-09-22 10:30+07' + interval '360 seconds'),
  ('77777777-0000-0000-0000-000000000117', 2, 'FollowUp', 'How do mocks help unit tests?', 'They provide data.', 'audio/000032/q3-t2.webm', timestamptz '2026-09-22 10:30+07' + interval '370 seconds', timestamptz '2026-09-22 10:30+07' + interval '460 seconds'),
  ('77777777-0000-0000-0000-000000000118', 1, 'Main', 'What information should a good bug report contain?', 'It needs a title, the steps taken and the wrong result.', 'audio/000032/q4-t1.webm', timestamptz '2026-09-22 10:30+07' + interval '470 seconds', timestamptz '2026-09-22 10:30+07' + interval '550 seconds'),
  ('77777777-0000-0000-0000-000000000118', 2, 'FollowUp', 'Besides the steps to reproduce, what information about the environment does a bug report need?', 'The browser, the operating system and the application version.', 'audio/000032/q4-t2.webm', timestamptz '2026-09-22 10:30+07' + interval '560 seconds', timestamptz '2026-09-22 10:30+07' + interval '639 seconds'),
  ('77777777-0000-0000-0000-000000000119', 1, 'Main', 'Explain the difference between black-box and white-box testing.', 'Black-box testing is based on the specification without knowing the code, using techniques like equivalence partitioning and boundary value analysis. White-box testing is based on the code structure, for example statement coverage and branch coverage. Black-box tests are usually written by testers, white-box tests by developers when writing unit tests.', 'audio/000033/q1-t1.webm', timestamptz '2026-09-22 11:00+07' + interval '30 seconds', timestamptz '2026-09-22 11:00+07' + interval '144 seconds'),
  ('77777777-0000-0000-0000-000000000120', 1, 'Main', 'Explain equivalence partitioning and boundary value analysis, with an example.', 'Partitioning splits the inputs into groups and tests one value per group. Boundary values test the start and end of a range.', 'audio/000033/q2-t1.webm', timestamptz '2026-09-22 11:00+07' + interval '154 seconds', timestamptz '2026-09-22 11:00+07' + interval '201 seconds'),
  ('77777777-0000-0000-0000-000000000120', 2, 'FollowUp', 'For an age field from 18 to 60, which boundary values would you pick?', 'I would pick 17, 18, 60 and 61.', 'audio/000033/q2-t2.webm', timestamptz '2026-09-22 11:00+07' + interval '211 seconds', timestamptz '2026-09-22 11:00+07' + interval '255 seconds'),
  ('77777777-0000-0000-0000-000000000121', 1, 'Main', 'How is a unit test different from an integration test? Why do we need mocks?', 'A unit test checks a small unit such as one function or class; it is fast and isolated. An integration test checks several components working together, such as the API with a real database. Mocks replace external dependencies like the database or an AI service, so unit tests stay isolated, fast and stable.', 'audio/000033/q3-t1.webm', timestamptz '2026-09-22 11:00+07' + interval '265 seconds', timestamptz '2026-09-22 11:00+07' + interval '320 seconds'),
  ('77777777-0000-0000-0000-000000000122', 1, 'Main', 'What information should a good bug report contain?', 'Just write that there is a bug.', 'audio/000033/q4-t1.webm', timestamptz '2026-09-22 11:00+07' + interval '330 seconds', timestamptz '2026-09-22 11:00+07' + interval '370 seconds'),
  ('77777777-0000-0000-0000-000000000122', 2, 'FollowUp', 'Besides the steps to reproduce, what information about the environment does a bug report need?', 'That is not needed.', 'audio/000033/q4-t2.webm', timestamptz '2026-09-22 11:00+07' + interval '380 seconds', timestamptz '2026-09-22 11:00+07' + interval '458 seconds'),
  ('77777777-0000-0000-0000-000000000123', 1, 'Main', 'Explain the difference between black-box and white-box testing.', 'Black-box testing is based on the specification without knowing the code, using techniques like equivalence partitioning and boundary value analysis. White-box testing is based on the code structure, for example statement coverage and branch coverage. Black-box tests are usually written by testers, white-box tests by developers when writing unit tests.', 'audio/000034/q1-t1.webm', timestamptz '2026-09-22 11:30+07' + interval '30 seconds', timestamptz '2026-09-22 11:30+07' + interval '121 seconds'),
  ('77777777-0000-0000-0000-000000000124', 1, 'Main', 'Explain equivalence partitioning and boundary value analysis, with an example.', 'Partitioning splits the inputs into groups and tests one value per group. Boundary values test the start and end of a range.', 'audio/000034/q2-t1.webm', timestamptz '2026-09-22 11:30+07' + interval '131 seconds', timestamptz '2026-09-22 11:30+07' + interval '184 seconds'),
  ('77777777-0000-0000-0000-000000000124', 2, 'FollowUp', 'For an age field from 18 to 60, which boundary values would you pick?', 'I would pick 17, 18, 60 and 61.', 'audio/000034/q2-t2.webm', timestamptz '2026-09-22 11:30+07' + interval '194 seconds', timestamptz '2026-09-22 11:30+07' + interval '304 seconds'),
  ('77777777-0000-0000-0000-000000000125', 1, 'Main', 'How is a unit test different from an integration test? Why do we need mocks?', 'A unit test checks a small unit such as one function or class; it is fast and isolated. An integration test checks several components working together, such as the API with a real database. Mocks replace external dependencies like the database or an AI service, so unit tests stay isolated, fast and stable.', 'audio/000034/q3-t1.webm', timestamptz '2026-09-22 11:30+07' + interval '314 seconds', timestamptz '2026-09-22 11:30+07' + interval '382 seconds'),
